  "notes": [
    "Source: CLAUDE.md. Speeds entered as knots, stored in m/s.",
    "Manufacturer speeds published in mph, converted to knots (x 0.869), rounded down to whole knots.",
    "Max weight 816 kg is the aerobatic category limit.",
    "Official figures (americanchampionaircraft.com). Fuel 151 L is usable (40 US gal); total 43 gal / 163 L. Cruise 141 mph at 75% power.",
    "Fuel density 0.72 kg/L (avgas 100LL).",
    "Gear and inertia are Stage 3 engineering estimates, to be refined in Stage 5.",
    "Gear: mains 0.45 m ahead of CG, 1.9 m track, toe brakes; steerable tailwheel (+/-30 deg) 5.05 m behind the mains; about 11 deg nose-up on the ground.",
    "Struts sized for ~5 cm static compression on the mains and ~0.5 critical damping.",
    "Inertia from Roskam radii of gyration for light singles (Rx 0.248, Ry 0.338, Rz 0.393) with an assumed 7.0 m length.",
    "Stage 5 flight model (estimates tuned to the CLAUDE.md targets; see docs/STATUS.md):",
    "Aero: near-symmetric NACA 1412-type section (zero-lift alpha about -1 deg), CLmax 1.42, CLmin -1.17 (good inverted); wing incidence 1.5 deg; CD0 0.038 (fixed gear, struts, aerobatic fittings), whole-aircraft e 0.72.",
    "Roll damping fades and reverses between 18 and 35 deg alpha (wing autorotation, the engine of a spin); yaw damping falls in the deep stall.",
    "Propeller: Hartzell 74 in two-blade constant-speed, governed 2000-2700 rpm; CT/CP at reference pitch, scaled with blade pitch.",
    "Engine: Lycoming AEIO-360-H1B, 180 hp at 2700 rpm, fuel injected with inverted fuel and oil (limits.invertedSystems).",
    "Rudder power falls to about 40% beyond 35 deg alpha (fin in the stalled wing's wake), which sets a realistic spin rate.",
    "Pitch break past the stall (CmExtra) is sized so full aft stick without rotation settles just above the stall (about 26 deg alpha): no stable deep stall. In a spin the inertial pitch-up from roll and yaw rates holds a higher alpha.",
    "Panel (Stage 7): six-pack plus engine gauges and G-meter. Markings from CLAUDE.md speeds (green 49-139 kt, yellow 139-173 kt, red line 173 kt), red line 2,700 rpm, +6/-5 g; Lycoming CHT limit 260 C (500 F)."
